+/* Vessel: FEX_SILENTLOG, read from the environment instead of from the config.
+ *
+ * Init() runs before any config layer has been loaded, on every path that
+ * reaches it. The two Windows modules call it from ProcessInit ahead of
+ * FEX::Config::LoadConfig (ARM64EC/Module.cpp:657, WOW64/Module.cpp:519), and
+ * FEXOfflineCompiler calls it from the first two statements of main() with only
+ * FEXCore::Config::Initialize() done -- patches/fex/0001, which is there
+ * because without it this function faulted on a null MetaLayer. Initialize()
+ * creates that layer; it loads nothing into it. So the FEX_CONFIG_OPT below can
+ * only ever return the compiled-in default, and that default is *true*
+ * (FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in:387-389).
+ *
+ * Which means Init() returns without installing a handler, and nothing calls
+ * Init() a second time, so every LogMan message in the process is discarded for
+ * the rest of its life -- EFmt included, and the message half of
+ * ERROR_AND_DIE_FMT included. FEX_SILENTLOG=0 has never been able to change
+ * that on any of the three entry points.
+ *
+ * How it was located rather than assumed, 2026-08-14: FEXOfflineCompiler64.exe
+ * was run under Wine with no guest process, nothing else in the prefix, and
+ * FEX_SILENTLOG=0 in its environment. It printed "Parsed 26 codemap entries for
+ * .../amd_fidelityfx_loader_dx12.dll" and "Compiling code..." -- which are
+ * fmt::print, not LogMan (FEXOfflineCompiler/Main.cpp:596 and :519) -- and then
+ * nothing at all for 180 s until the timeout killed it. The LogMan lines that
+ * path emits between those two prints, "Relocated image {:X} -> {:X}" and
+ * "Mapped image: {} @ {:X}" (Main.cpp:284 and :342), were absent. Two prints
+ * present and two logs missing from the same twenty lines of code is the whole
+ * proof; nothing about the hang itself is claimed here.
+ *
+ * The environment wins over the config value rather than merging with it,
+ * because at this point there is no config value -- only a default. A caller
+ * who wants the default keeps it by not setting the variable.
+ *
+ * The conversion matches what FEX's own config layer would do to the same
+ * string, so the two cannot disagree: a config bool is
+ * strtoull(Value, nullptr, 0) cast to bool (FEXCore/Source/Common/StringConv.h
+ * :11-18), i.e. "a non-zero integer is true". Worth knowing before writing one:
+ * FEX_SILENTLOG=true parses as zero and therefore means *not* silent.
+ *
+ * Hand-rolled rather than calling strtoull, because this file compiles into
+ * CommonWindows, which links into libarm64ecfex.dll against FEX's own minimal
+ * CRT -- and that CRT has getenv (CRT/Misc.cpp:58) but no string-to-integer
+ * conversion of any kind (CRT/String.cpp). getenv is already relied on two
+ * functions above for VESSEL_TRACE, so the mechanism is proven on this path;
+ * strtoull would be a new link dependency. The digit scan is decimal only: a
+ * hexadecimal FEX_SILENTLOG=0x1 would read as false here and as true through
+ * the config layer, and nobody writes one for a flag. */
+std::optional<bool> SilentFromEnvironment() {
+  const char* Value = getenv("FEX_SILENTLOG");
+  if (!Value) {
+    return std::nullopt;
+  }
+
+  std::string_view View {Value};
+  while (!View.empty() && (View.front() == ' ' || View.front() == '\t')) {
+    View.remove_prefix(1);
+  }
+  if (!View.empty() && (View.front() == '+' || View.front() == '-')) {
+    View.remove_prefix(1);
+  }
+
+  bool NonZero = false;
+  for (const char C : View) {
+    if (C < '0' || C > '9') {
+      break;
+    }
+    NonZero = NonZero || C != '0';
+  }
+  return NonZero;
+}
